y parts. We denote\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⟹ & {u}^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{t} & ⟹ & v=\\int {v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t={e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, applying the integration by parts formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t & =uv{|}_{0}^{3}-{\\int }_{0}^{3}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t{e}^{t}){|}_{0}^{3}-{\\int }_{0}^{3}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(3{e}^{3}-0{e}^{0})-{e}^{t}{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =3{e}^{3}-({e}^{3}-1) \\\\  & =2{e}^{3}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's now examine the statements:\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. This is as a result of the above calculations.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since the inner product is not zero, our vectors are not orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534768 true] [17592186308969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308970 13194139534768 true] [17592186308969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308971 13194139534768 true] [17592186308969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308972 13194139534768 true] [17592186308969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308973 13194139534768 true] [17592186308969 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308974 13194139534768 true] [17592186308969 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534768 true] [17592186308969 1041 "selection" 13194139534768 true] [17592186308969 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308972 13194139534768 true] [17592186308969 1110 #uuid "c6030c2d-9773-598e-b8be-79fa3d4c9985" 13194139534768 true] [17592186308970 1034 "II and III only" 13194139534768 true] [17592186308970 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534768 true] [17592186308970 1111 #uuid "67cd2901-db7d-5a1f-ae27-2ba0b38c96a6" 13194139534768 true] [17592186308971 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534768 true] [17592186308971 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534768 true] [17592186308971 1111 #uuid "9c34072c-5988-5515-a7ce-d328e36106f4" 13194139534768 true] [17592186308972 1034 "I only" 13194139534768 true] [17592186308972 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534768 true] [17592186308